Here's a simple Delphi program that can load and execute Python code using the Python for Windows Embedded Distribution (PEWD).

First, you need to download and install Python for Windows Embedded Distribution (PEWD) from the following link: <https://github.com/cgoldberg/python-for-windows-embedded>

After installing PEWD, create a new Delphi project and add the following code:

```delphi
program PythonRunner;

{$APPTYPE CONSOLE}

uses
  SysUtils,
  ActiveX,
  ComObj;

function Py_Initialize(): HRESULT; stdcall; external 'pythonXY.dll' name 'Py_Initialize';
function PyRun_SimpleString(Command: PAnsiChar): Integer; stdcall; external 'pythonXY.dll' name 'PyRun_SimpleString';
function Py_Finalize(): Integer; stdcall; external 'pythonXY.dll' name 'Py_Finalize';

var
  PythonCode: string;
  PythonDLLPath: string;
  ResultCode: Integer;
begin
  try
    // Set the path to the PythonXY.dll file, adjust it according to your installation.
    PythonDLLPath := 'C:\PythonXY\pythonXY.dll';

    // Initialize the Python interpreter
    if Py_Initialize() <> S_OK then
    begin
      Writeln('Failed to initialize Python interpreter.');
      Halt(1);
    end;

    // Input Python code
    Write('Enter Python code: ');
    Readln(PythonCode);

    // Execute the Python code
    ResultCode := PyRun_SimpleString(PAnsiChar(PythonCode));

    // Check if the Python code execution was successful
    if ResultCode = 0 then
      Writeln('Python code executed successfully.')
    else
      Writeln('Python code execution failed with error code: ', ResultCode);

    // Finalize the Python interpreter
    Py_Finalize();

  except
    on E: Exception do
      Writeln(E.ClassName, ': ', E.Message);
  end;
end.
```

Replace `'C:\PythonXY\pythonXY.dll'` with the path to your `pythonXY.dll` file.

This program initializes the Python interpreter, takes Python code as input, executes it, and then finalizes the interpreter. Note that this method only works for simple Python scripts and has some limitations, but it serves as a starting point for executing Python code from Delphi.

Make sure to set the correct path to the `pythonXY.dll` file in the `PythonDLLPath` variable. Compile and run the program, enter some Python code, and see the output in the console.

