  <XYPlot width={400} height={300}>
    <RectSeries data={data} style={shadedRegionStyle} />
    <XAxis />
    <YAxis />
  </XYPlot>
);

export default App;
```

In this example, the `RectSeries` component is used to draw rectangles on the plot. The `data` array specifies the coordinates of the rectangles, where `x0` and `x` represent the left and right x-coordinates, and `y` represents the y-coordinate.

The `shadedRegionStyle` object defines the style of the shaded region, including its opacity and fill color.

By rendering the `RectSeries` component before the axes, the shaded region will be displayed behind the other plot elements.

